WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.337
Administrative units replace
OU delegation, in three tiers.

2
00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:08.025
Tier 1 is read-only visibility,
and its reader roles

3
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:11.625
can't be scoped to a unit,
so they sit at tenant scope.

4
00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:14.869
Tier 2 is the department
unit, whose rule lists the

5
00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:19.063
department's organization codes,
the same roll-up its group uses.

6
00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:25.150
Tier 3 is the division unit, created on
demand, reading the division code in slot 6.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:30.103
Scoped roles go to role-assignable groups
whose members are eligible through PIM,

8
00:00:30.103 --> 00:00:33.162
and each unit is created
before the groups it holds.

9
00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:35.988
The decision you can't
undo is restriction.

10
00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:40.888
Decide it before the unit exists, and
default to no, because restriction takes

11
00:00:40.888 --> 00:00:46.249
members out of PIM, entitlement management,
Lifecycle Workflows and access reviews.

12
00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:50.987
VK-DG-07 reads two small files:
one maps each unit to its group,

13
00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:55.917
and flags a unit whose rule doesn't
match; the other records why

14
00:00:55.917 --> 00:01:01.200
a unit is restricted, and flags
any restricted unit with no reason.
